<node id="ISS Office">
  <data key="d0">ISS Office</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The ISS Office (Office of International Relations) is located at the International Hall on the Humanities and Social Sciences Campus in Seoul.&lt;SEP&gt;The ISS Office is responsible for handling scholarship applications, approvals, and communication regarding tuition benefits.&lt;SEP&gt;The ISS Office is responsible for managing applications, payments, and issuing acceptance letters for the program.&lt;SEP&gt;The ISS Office is responsible for managing the International Summer Semester program at Sungkyunkwan University.&lt;SEP&gt;The ISS Office supports students participating in the ISS program by providing necessary documents for visa applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-16cbcaef78bf936a584694124dc66335&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee86da05db26bc26419fc8a7bb74a441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b62f790fb108b029553fbfebbf5d074b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce6e95b17114e2024e143001cc21784c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7f2c602b863e29ddf14e816b366b63a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1749108482</data>
</node>
<node id="Re-registration Benefit">
  <data key="d0">Re-registration Benefit</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Re-registration Benefit provides a 30% discount on tuition fees for students who have previously participated in an ISS program.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7f2c602b863e29ddf14e816b366b63a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1749108190</data>
</node>
<node id="Kingo Family Scholarship">
  <data key="d0">Kingo Family Scholarship</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">The Kingo Family Scholarship offers a 50% tuition discount for students with a parent who is an SKKU alumnus or employed at SKKU as full-time faculty or staff.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b7f2c602b863e29ddf14e816b366b63a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1749108190</data>
</node>
<node id="SKKU">
  <data key="d0">SKKU</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">SKKU (Sungkyunkwan University) is an academic institution offering various facilities and services for students, including cafeterias, libraries, gyms, medical clinics, and banking services.&lt;SEP&gt;Sungkyunkwan University (SKKU) is a prestigious academic institution located in South Korea, with campuses in Seoul and Suwon. Renowned for its excellence in education, SKKU offers a diverse range of academic programs and services, including courses such as "Understanding Global Conflict," "Digital Strategies in Media and Communication," and Korean language courses provided through the Sungkyun Language Institute. The university also organizes specialized programs like the International Summer Semester (ISS) and supports its students with comprehensive services such as internet access, postal services, dining options, healthcare, and student housing.

SKKU is represented by distinguished faculty members, including Jong-Bom Chay, Young-Han Kim, and Gaya Nadarajan, who contribute to its academic and research excellence. The university is also deeply committed to its community, offering initiatives like the Kingo Family Scholarship for alumni and staff, as well as group health insurance for its students. Additionally, students actively participate in events such as the Kingo Walkathon, fostering a vibrant campus culture.

As an institution, SKKU provides robust academic policies, grading systems, and course syllabi to ensure a high-quality educational experience. Its dedication to holistic student support and innovative programs cements its reputation as a leading university in South Korea.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-60e103e0807596240e5b01989129e459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602992be1a3529cb1f1681276e7b4baf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91964e73ecc4c81dd05b467f5d7acf2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c431f4ad10d3d717f10b55808b36752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf623025e86ce4ba3f16427634642e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e806d65c28cb060fad6e0ba22951f523&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bfebb1097a2e216f52589d6879b9f3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1acca9611ca93fee0e67de9292aa2f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65141db8aa8fdc715a2f319ecdc219df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee86da05db26bc26419fc8a7bb74a441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7f2c602b863e29ddf14e816b366b63a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c40b5297d8a88640a41d101935859d</data>
