<node id="ISS Program">
  <data key="d0">ISS Program</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The ISS Program, also known as the International Summer Semester (ISS), is an academic initiative hosted by Sungkyunkwan University (SKKU) in South Korea. Designed primarily for international students, the program offers a diverse selection of structured academic courses across multiple disciplines, including Computer &amp; Data Science, Business &amp; Economics, Social Science &amp; Humanities, Engineering, and Korean Studies &amp; Korean Language. Participants also have the option to engage in the ISS Research Internship as part of their academic experience. The program spans a maximum duration of four weeks and requires participants to adhere to South Korea's visa regulations. In addition to academic coursework, students gain access to SKKU's campus facilities, making it a comprehensive educational and cultural experience.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f59ec17f08b561b76ce546e31586bb9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c431f4ad10d3d717f10b55808b36752&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf623025e86ce4ba3f16427634642e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f24e89350b05126a3c95d917db3b098&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce6e95b17114e2024e143001cc21784c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5c40b5297d8a88640a41d101935859d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1749108506</data>
</node>
<node id="Housing Options">
  <data key="d0">Housing Options</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Housing Options include on-campus accommodations at Seoul and Suwon campuses, with choices of double or single occupancy during the ISS Research Internship.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0f24e89350b05126a3c95d917db3b098</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
